    //Green Sheet Slime:
    [['This little puddle of green goop brings back memories of how I ended up here. This was the first creature from in the sheets that I saw.', 5], ['They seem to be relatively harmless compared to other creatures here, minding their own business until disturbed. Often residing in the cracks throughout the ground, they spring up if anything gets too close.', 15], ["I've seen this happen when a Red Sheet Slime provoked a Green Sheet Slime, and they didn't seem hostile to each other in the slightest, implying that all colors of Sheet Slimes are somehow related.", 40], ['They even seemed quite happy to have found each other, almost "mixing" some of their liquids together. I am currently unsure what sort of purpose this mixing might serve, but I hope I can find out in the future since it seems like a wonder of sheet-based biology that is unknown (at least to me) back in the real world.', 75], ["Their goopy insides don't seem to have anything resembling organs, which makes me wonder how they can survive. Are they effectively just a scaled up ameoba?", 135], ["I haven't personally witnessed them eat anything, but I would imagine they simply absorb and dissolve their prey. I really wish I could study them closer, but despite how harmless they can appear, I still don't feel safe enough to get a sample of their slime.", 200]],
    //Red Sheet Slime:
    [['This little bugger is much more aggresive than their green counterparts, often actively seeking combat.', 5], ['Rather than attacking their foe directly, they use some sort of magic to siphon the life energy of their still-living prey.', 15], ['While this magic is powerful, it does not come without consequence, as these slimes are much more frail than others.', 40], ['They circumvent this weakness by sneaking up on their prey, often dropping from the ceiling to ambush their target.', 75], ['Watching them from a distance shows that they travel around much more than the other slime types.', 135], ["While the green and yellow varieties tend to stay to themselves, I don't think I've ever seen a Red Sheet Slime retrace its steps. They always travel, forever hunting.", 200]],
    //Yellow Sheet Slime:
    [["The final color of Sheet Slime that I have seen here, and it's a much more welcome sight than the others.", 5], ['From what I can tell, these slimes appear to be herbivors, which means that they are one of the few creatures here that I know is not hunting me down.', 12], ["They avoid combat as best that they can, only fighting when escape isn't an option, which it rarely is due to their slime being much stiffer and harder to move.", 25], ["They lack any true offensive options and as such, resort to simply throwing some of their goop to try to scare away their enemy. This is obviously unsustainable, but they don't really have any other options, I suppose.", 40], ['I almost feel bad for them, they seem so helpless all by themselves.', 65], ['On one occasion I actually witnessed a slime feeding on the moss from a Macro Golem.', 100], ['I am unsure whether or not the golem is the source of the moss or even if if the moss here acts as it does in the real world, but it was very interesting to see some cross-species symbiosis like this.', 140], ["It reminds me of a species of fish that cleans the inside of a shark's mouth. The golem even directly benefits from this due to the moss often clogging the golem's arms, causing them to not move as effectively.", 200]],
    //Cellyfish:
    [['A strange floating... Thing? It seems to resemble a jellyfish, but it is much more aggressive.', 5], ['It actively hunts prey with its stinging tentacles, powered by pure electricity, seemingly drawn from the air around it.', 15], ['Though it is aggressive, it is not durable, and it cannot see, so it often ends up in fights that it has no true hope of winning, especially due to its lack of defense.', 40], ['They seem to like to cluster together, often forming large "herds". These herds make up for their individual weaknesses, power in numbers and all that.', 75], ["Often the herds also have a rather strong leader. I've heard booming thunders when a large herd is nearby that no single Cellyfish could make on its own, so I can only assume that the leader must be responsible.", 135], ["If I ever encounter one of these leaders, I just hope that they aren't as strong as they are loud...", 200]],
    //Adder:
    [['(Currently no notes. Will be added in the future)', 0]],
    //Cell Crawler:
    [['A strange creature... Though not very threatening. They seem to quite literally be a cell that sprouted legs and came to life.', 5], ['The way they crawl around is very unnerving, very reminiscent of bugs.', 15], ["Speaking of bugs, from what little I've seen, they act seemingly quite like ants, even biting with conealed mandibles.", 40], ["These foragers often place resources inside their container-like bodies to carry them to some sort of hive, though I've never even seen this hive.", 75], ['Although, if I know anything from bugs back in the real world, I know better than to traipse right into an insect colony.', 135], ['And I fret to find out what sort of queen these creatures might have. ', 200]],
